{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Review",
  "description": "When source code files are edited, analyze the modified code for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generate suggestions for improving code quality while maintaining existing functionality, focusing on readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/**/*.py"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the recently modified code for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. Code smells: duplicated logic, overly long functions, deep nesting, magic numbers, dead code.\n2. Design patterns: suggest applicable patterns that could improve structure (e.g., strategy, factory, observer) without over-engineering.\n3. Best practices: proper error handling, type hints, docstrings, naming conventions, SOLID principles.\n4. Readability: unclear variable names, complex expressions that could be simplified, missing comments for non-obvious logic.\n5. Maintainability: tight coupling, missing abstractions, hardcoded values that should be configurable.\n6. Performance: unnecessary iterations, inefficient data structures, opportunities for caching or lazy evaluation.\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions. Do not rewrite the entire file — only highlight specific areas and recommend targeted changes. Preserve existing functionality."
  }
}